{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "18", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "23", "M": "56", "S": "59"}}, "news": [{"title": "Kochi: Crores spent on slum rehabilitation, yet P&T Colony families without homes", "para": "Residents of P&T Colony have been moved to apartments now considered unsafe, suffering from significant construction defects like cracked walls and wastewater leaks. Families consistently raise alarms with the Greater Cochin Development Authority, but progress remains stagnant. Compounding their plight are bureaucratic hold-ups in issuing vital certificates for other families, leaving many still in limbo. Despite ongoing discussions, a resolution seems distant for those impacted.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/kochi-crores-spent-on-slum-rehabilitation-yet-pt-colony-families-without-homes/135029047?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-302424/135029047.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Himachal Pradesh HC flags illegal-height Barog projects, seeks 10-year state-wide land deal data", "para": "The Himachal Pradesh high court has instructed the government to furnish an in-depth report on land purchase permits. Concerns were voiced about towering multi-storey structures breaching height regulations in Barog, Solan district. The court seeks clarity on permissions issued under Section 118 of the HP Tenancy and Land Reforms Act and demands transparency on both approved and rejected applications.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/himachal-pradesh-hc-flags-illegal-height-barog-projects-seeks-10-year-state-wide-land-deal-data/135029003?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-188662/135029003.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Joint property owners in Bengaluru can now split A-eKhata online, get separate records", "para": "In a bid to simplify property management, the Greater Bengaluru Authority has unveiled an online service designed for joint property owners. With this service, holders of joint A-eKhatas can easily obtain distinct e-khatas, enabling them to handle their property affairs on their own. A sub-division fee based on the guidance value will be implemented. This effort seeks to streamline property transactions in Bengaluru, reducing the need for extensive manual processes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/joint-property-owners-in-bengaluru-can-now-split-a-ekhata-online-get-separate-records/135028901?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-103/135028901.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}]}